From: JZ Loh <ljzyx86@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: es8389: keep the powered codec accessible on restart

The SDK shutdown sequence isolates the codec's control interface. On
systems whose codec supply remains enabled during a warm restart, the next
probe cannot read the chip ID and subsequent ALSA register accesses fail
with -ENXIO. Power cycling restores access; panic and watchdog resets,
which skip device_shutdown(), also retain access.

Cancel the delayed state worker on every shutdown, but reserve the deep
power-down sequence for halt and power-off. A restarting kernel will probe
and initialize the still-powered codec. This does not add board GPIOs or
change the normal power-off sequence.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/es8389.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/es8389.c
@@ -832,6 +832,10 @@ static void es8389_i2c_shutdown(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&es8389->state_work);
 
+	/* The control interface must survive a restart without a supply cycle. */
+	if (system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART)
+		return;
+
 	regmap_write(es8389->regmap, ES8389_MASTER_MODE_REG01, 0x28);
 	regmap_write(es8389->regmap, ES8389_HPSW_REG69, 0x00);
 	regmap_write(es8389->regmap, ES8389_VMID_REG60, 0x00);
